m is currently paused, our near-term capital needs are primarily driven by our UAS growth plan and the development of our unmanned systems and domestic manufacturing initiatives.","context":"Our ability to continue funding our operations and execute our long-term development strategy depends on our ability to maintain sufficient liquidity and obtain additional capital over time.","section":"ITEM 1A: RISK FACTORS","block":257,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-043785","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026043785/ea0279149-10k_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/091060cf94e269f5a0c80446269ef02005fbb5a7f6ff428831dcd60e92b6b62d.bin","sha256":"091060cf94e269f5a0c80446269ef02005fbb5a7f6ff428831dcd60e92b6b62d"}},{"id":"8fb744c630db0c899691fccc19458bccfd17e875345fa78148f60e3bf7d16292","quote":"Our ability to obtain additional financing will depend on many factors, including market conditions, investor demand, our operating performance, and broader economic conditions. If we are unable to obtain additional capital when needed or on acceptable terms, we may be required to delay or scale back certain development programs, reduce operating expenditures, or modify our business strategy, any of which could materially adversely affect our business, financial condition and results of operations.","context":"Our operations have historically generated net losses and negative operating cash flows, and we have incurred significant cumulative losses since inception. Although we believe our current liquidity is sufficient to fund operations for at least the next twelve months, we will require additional capital over time to support the growth of our UAS distribution and services businesses via acquisitions and, if we decide to resume the TriFan 600 program, the continued development, certification and commercialization of the TriFan 600 aircraft. Because the TriFan 600 program is currently paused, our near-term capital needs are primarily driven by our UAS growth plan and the development of our unmanned systems and domestic manufacturing initiatives.","section":"ITEM 1A: RISK FACTORS","block":258,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-043785","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026043785/ea0279149-10k_xtiaero.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/091060cf94e269f5a0c80446269ef02005fbb5a7f6ff428831dcd60e92b6b62d.bin","sha256":"091060cf94e269f5a0c80446269ef02005fbb5a7f6ff428831dcd60e92b6b62d"}},{"id":"5ca06697d9f760d55e66c79f1a45170e2fb5e4a7ac0ecbceb8d5910784301f0a","quote":"Our UAS business operates in a rapidly evolving market and is subject to risks related to changes in technology, customer demand, regulatory developments and procurement requirements.","context":"Our ability to obtain additional financing will depend on many factors, including market conditions, investor demand, our operating performance, and broader economic conditions. If we are unable to obtain additional capital when needed or on acceptable terms, we may be required to delay or scale back certain development programs, reduce operating expenditures, or modify our business strategy, any of which could materially adversely affect our business, financial condition and results of operations.","section":"ITEM 1A: RISK FACTORS","block":259,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-043785","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-15","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001529113","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1529113/000121390026043785/ea0279149-10k_xtiaero.htm","ra